Joel,

Mateo looped me in (Tessera ticket #4471). Short version: this was on our side, it's fixed, and you should be able to log in now.

- Impact: every SP-initiated login for your Okta app returned 400 since the app was created. Nobody in the pilot group could have got in.
- Root cause: attribute mapping. Our ACS was looking for an attribute literally named `email`; the profile in the setup guide maps it as `login`. The guide and the ACS disagreed with each other, which is our bug, not your config.
- Fix: the ACS now accepts `email`, `login`, or the NameID when it's in emailAddress format. Shipped 16:20 PT. No change needed on the Okta app.
- Follow-up: we'll correct the setup guide this week.

Could you retest with one pilot user and let us know? If it still fails, send me the Okta System Log entry and I'll look at it tonight.

Jordan

On Sun, Sep 6, 2026 at 11:20 AM, Joel Brennan <joel.brennan@halberd.com> wrote:
> Hi Tessera support,
>
> We're standing up the pilot group ahead of Tuesday and SAML is failing for every user in the Halberd-Tessera-Pilot Okta group. Details:
